      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is usage for Encoder, our persistent input surface can be utilized by multiple encoder instances(not simultaneously) one by one. Each encoder could have different consumer usage. (e.g. s/w encoder and h/w encoder)\n\nAnd of course, there will be cleaning-up and set-up regarding disconnecting from the previous encoder and connecting the current encoder.\n\nconsumer usage is retrieved from the encoder instance around here, and set to `config-\u003emIsConfig-\u003emUsage` in just a little bit below.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp;drc\u003d454ac2b3e6024e004f7665dc07b6c3d23d1fd4fb;l\u003d1597\n\nAnd the retrieved usage is set here.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/module/bqhelper/GraphicBufferSource.cpp;drc\u003d454ac2b3e6024e004f7665dc07b6c3d23d1fd4fb;l\u003d1194\n\n(called from here https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp;drc\u003d454ac2b3e6024e004f7665dc07b6c3d23d1fd4fb;l\u003d507 )",
